<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7431"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 11:01 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Melissa, aka FBIknowsu, in the AMW board tells the story of working in Germany in the 1980s with a mysterious man. They worked in an aviation-type company. She and another co-worker/friend drove this man somewhere in town one weekend. It turned out there was a murder at the same place where they had left the man that weekend. <BR> <BR>She knew that the person they gave a ride to had killed the man, who was found hanging by the neck from the ceiling, and there was semen all over the place. <BR> <BR>Upon her return to the USA, she went to live in  Georgia. And, she signed up for match.com, a dating service. She was getting emails and PMs from a man for some time, then one day she bothered to check the match.com profile - it was the same man who she thought committed the murder in Germany. <BR> <BR>She goes on to say that she notified the FBI, her local police, KAKE TV, and other news and law enforcement agencies, but nobody was taking her seriously.  <BR> <BR>She said she was afraid and moved out of her county and went to live in another where nobody knew her. Then one night she saw the same man in a restaurant sitting on the bar right across from her, staring at her. She says that the man had two other acquaintances who may or may not know what he&#39;s  up to, but she thinks they do. <BR> <BR>Most everyone think this woman has lost it, and she&#39;s just a case of extreme paranoia caused by too much BTK bulletin boards. She may have in fact been stalked by the man, since these things happen often. But, she has no proof that he is BTK. <BR> <BR>I just thought on mentioning this here, as AMW wants to talk to her, and it seems that after posting on AMW, authorities are taking her more seriously. She has armed herself, and is taunting BTK to go get her. <BR> <BR>Pretty wicked stuff. <BR> <BR>:|<!--/Text--></td></tr>
